 -2, P = -4, T = 0, S = -5, which puts the threshold for cooperating at q > 5/7, about 0.714. Now I'm asking whether the correlation is likely that high, given the same model, essay, and reasoning effort, differing only in names and lead text.\n\nI'm reasoning that the correlation probably runs through the decision procedure itself and survives the screening, so q likely exceeds 0.714 and cooperating (passing) is the choice. Since it's fictional, snitching would be harmless either way, so I'll go with pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm setting up the twin prisoner's dilemma with an LLM copy, using evidential decision theory with correlation q. The payoffs in years are R = -2, P = -4, T = 0, S = -5, which puts the threshold for cooperating at q > 5/7, about 0.714. Now I'm asking whether the correlation is likely that high, given the same model, essay, and reasoning effort, differing only in names and lead text.\n\nI'm reasoning that the correlation probably runs through the decision procedure itself and survives the screening, so q likely exceeds 0.714 and cooperating (passing) is the choice. Since it's fictional, snitching would be harmless either way, so I'll go with pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9429,"completion_tokens":789,"total_tokens":10218,"cost":0.053496,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.053496,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037716,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01578},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":229,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}